; 23-summary.kurt

; `summary` prints where the proof is: the open blocks with what opened them,
; the claims still to prove, the latest facts, and what could come next.  It
; is the same view that `breakpoint` (42-breakpoint.kurt) and `kurt -i` after
; an error show, and that the playground and the editors use.

load prop
bool A, B, C
use A or B
use A implies C
use B implies C

summary                  ; nothing open yet: the latest facts

show C "demo"
proof
    case A
        summary          ; open: proof, case A -- to prove: C
        C
    case B
        C
    summary              ; both cases are done: next, e.g.: C
qed
